"""Shared closed/free separator dispatch from semantic Bundle records.

Kind zero retains the checked closed assembly. Kind one consumes a complete
pair of free approaches. Kind two follows complete closed member chains;
kind three follows complete chains to their genuine free approaches. Kind four
fills a declared member prefix ending at an original crossing Street, while its
remaining Bundle extents stay unclaimed. Kind five ends at explicitly declared
selection cuts, retaining each member's endpoint role and original Section ID.
Each accepted local fill restores every previous
public vertex key and face owner; its new cap and interior receive Bundle
identities. A failed fill adds a diagnostic, without adding loose cap vertices
or removing valid pavement. The caller must also prove semantic ownership with
curved_separator_contract_nodes.registry with the same free_ends/chained/
free_chains/regions/selection_ends capabilities. Geometry dispatch alone is not an ownership check.
"""
